{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON array of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first, each with two members: ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it is, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, as "},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds it; the record’s own "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"\"0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and no other device","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its unique users are sessions. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, rather than an event with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Mixpanel would attribute to no user,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events of the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as one, so a recovered record that Mixpanel had already stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The record’s vendor identifier and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" Mixpanel takes, and one too large for Mixpanel ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Mixpanel answers a request it reads with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. Mixpanel answers 200 as well when it ingests none of a request’s events: a wrong region,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored, so check the project’s Live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"View after setting it up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days: a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"older than that when it is sent, such as one a store kept through a long time offline, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted as delivered and not stored. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L83"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination":{"title":"HTTPDestination","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"title":"BatchEncoder","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/docume